#!/usr/bin/env bash
# Weekly MazingiraKenya Narrative-Disinfo queue — 2026-11-23
# Queues UNPUBLISHED drafts (published=false) into Supabase disinfo_items for admin review.
# This run wrote the 4 drafts via the connected Chrome (POST /rest/v1/disinfo_items, 201) because
# the Mac device-bridge shell cannot reach supabase.co (curl 403 from proxy on CONNECT this run).
# This script reproduces the same inserts anywhere Supabase IS reachable, via insert-disinfo-draft.mjs.
#   Usage: bash scripts/queue-disinfo-2026-11-23.sh
set -euo pipefail
cd "$(dirname "$0")/.."

run() { node scripts/insert-disinfo-draft.mjs "$1"; }

run "$(cat <<'JSON'
{"name":"Circulating after high-profile remarks dismissing El Niño forecasts (Kenya)","posted_at":"2026-11-23","verdict":"Minimisation / eroding trust in science","verdict_class":"vm","source_url":"https://www.nation.africa/kenya/news/ruto-versus-experts-questions-as-president-mocks-science-on-el-ni%C3%B1o-threat-5626522","source_label":"Nation.africa 'Ruto versus experts' (Oct 2026); WMO; Kenya Met (KMSA); Greenpeace Africa","body":"Kenya's weather experts keep shifting the El Niño timeline — first August, then September, then October — so the forecasters are just guessing, and their flood warnings (and climate science generally) can't be trusted.","rebuttal":"Seasonal forecasts are probabilities, not a timetable, and mocking them erodes trust exactly when early warnings save lives. President Ruto questioned the shifting onset at an Oct 2026 summit ('waiting for these rains involves guesswork'), echoing his 2023 line that 'God has decreed there will be no El Niño… just heavy rainfall' — remarks experts warned could undermine public trust in science. The facts: El Niño is a Pacific warming that loads the dice toward a wetter October–December in much of Kenya, but Kenya Met (KMSA) is explicit that it does NOT guarantee uniform, on-schedule heavy rain everywhere — some areas stay hot and dry. Uncertainty about the exact onset is normal and does not mean the warning is wrong: the WMO (Nov 2026) calls this El Niño 'firmly established and strengthening,' with near-100% persistence through February 2027, and Greenpeace Africa notes timing uncertainty does not strip a warning of value. The 2023 episode is the cautionary tale — dismissive messaging preceded floods that killed scores. Treat Kenya Met and NDOC advisories as the authority on evacuations and closures, not a politician's scepticism."}
JSON
)"

run "$(cat <<'JSON'
{"name":"Circulating on social media / climate-skeptic posts (fact-checked for African audiences)","posted_at":"2026-11-23","verdict":"Climate denial / data-manipulation claim","verdict_class":"vf","source_url":"https://www.carbonbrief.org/explainer-how-data-adjustments-affect-global-temperature-records","source_label":"Carbon Brief explainer on data adjustments; Berkeley Earth; NASA/NOAA; PesaCheck fact-check","body":"The 'official' global-warming trend is manufactured: scientists secretly 'adjust' and 'homogenise' the raw thermometer records to add warming that isn't really there. The raw data shows little or no warming.","rebuttal":"Adjustments are a published, peer-reviewed correction for known measurement artefacts — weather stations being moved or changed, swaps in instruments, shifts in the time of day readings were taken, and the urban heat-island effect — not a thumb on the scale. The decisive detail the talking point hides: globally, the NET effect of all adjustments REDUCES the long-term warming trend rather than inflating it, because older ship-based ocean measurements ran artificially warm and correcting them pulls the early record up and the trend down; land adjustments are small by comparison (Carbon Brief; NOAA). Every independent team — NASA, NOAA, the UK Met Office/Hadley, and Berkeley Earth — finds the same roughly 1.1–1.5°C of warming, and so does the raw, unadjusted data. Berkeley Earth is telling: it was founded partly by sceptics and part-funded by a Koch-linked foundation specifically to re-check the records, and it confirmed the warming. The signal is corroborated far beyond thermometers — warming oceans, shrinking ice sheets, rising seas, earlier springs. For East Africa the clearest 'thermometer' is the near-complete loss of ice on Mt Kenya and Kilimanjaro. 'The data is faked' is one of the oldest denial claims, and it fails on its own numbers."}
JSON
)"

run "$(cat <<'JSON'
{"name":"Circulating on social media during the El Niño floods (Kenya / East Africa)","posted_at":"2026-11-23","verdict":"Conspiracy / false attribution","verdict_class":"vf","source_url":"https://www.earth.com/news/climate-change-denial-historic-floods-are-not-caused-by-cloud-seeding/","source_label":"Earth.com; AFP 'cloud-seeding claims overshadow record floods worldwide'; WMO / Kenya Met","body":"The heavy El Niño rains and floods hitting Kenya and the region aren't natural — they're man-made, deliberately engineered through secret cloud seeding, HAARP or 'geoengineering' to cause disaster.","rebuttal":"This is a conspiracy theory recycled onto every major flood worldwide (Dubai 2024, Spain, Pakistan, the US), and it fails on the physics. Cloud seeding can only nudge clouds that are ALREADY present to drop marginally more precipitation over a small area; it cannot conjure a weather system, let alone a months-long rainy season across several countries, and HAARP (a closed ionospheric research facility) has no capacity to steer weather at all. The real, well-understood drivers are a strong El Niño combined with a warm western Indian Ocean (a positive Indian Ocean Dipole) — a pattern Kenya Met and the WMO forecast months in advance precisely because it is natural and predictable, with human-driven climate change loading the atmosphere with more moisture and intensifying the downpours. Blaming secret technology is not harmless: it displaces attention from drainage, early-warning and evacuation that actually save lives, and it is often paired with engagement-bait. Verify flood and evacuation information against Kenya Met and the National Disaster Operations Centre."}
JSON
)"

run "$(cat <<'JSON'
{"name":"Circulating in energy-policy and fossil-promotion content (COP31 period)","posted_at":"2026-11-23","verdict":"Misleading framing / fossil-fuel talking point","verdict_class":"vm","source_url":"https://news.mongabay.com/short-article/2026/05/new-report-questions-africas-oil-and-gas-promise/","source_label":"Narrative pushed by CO2 Coalition / 'energy apartheid' pieces (2026); context: Mongabay 'New report questions Africa's oil & gas promise', IRENA 2024, IEA","body":"Renewables are too unreliable and too expensive to power Africa's development, so the continent must keep expanding oil, gas and coal. Restricting African fossil fuels is 'energy apartheid,' and climate campaigners are keeping Africa poor.","rebuttal":"Energy poverty in Africa is real and urgent — but 'fossil fuels or nothing' is a false choice, and the 'energy apartheid' slogan is promoted heavily by fossil-funded groups such as the CO2 Coalition. The economics have flipped: IRENA found 91% of new renewable power built worldwide in 2024 was cheaper than the cheapest new fossil option, and solar-plus-storage now rivals or beats new gas; the IEA reports clean energy draws about two-thirds of global energy investment. On reliability and reach, distributed solar and mini-grids electrify rural African communities faster and more cheaply than large grid-tied fossil plants that never reached them in the first place. Meanwhile new analyses (e.g. Mongabay, May 2026) find that decades of oil and gas wealth have largely failed to deliver development in African producer states, instead exposing them to price shocks, debt and stranded-asset risk. Both goals — expanding access AND cutting emissions — point the same way: a renewables-led build-out, not a fossil lock-in sold as 'development.'"}
JSON
)"

echo "Queued 4 disinfo drafts (2026-11-23) — awaiting admin review."
